678 1100 "Express the Maclaurin series expansion for $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ given by\n\n$$\nx\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{6}}{5!}-\\frac{{x}^{8}}{7!}+⋯\n$$\n\nusing sigma notation." 13194139535379 true] [17592186346678 1113 #uuid "66708e85-e31b-5700-a1e3-46ef23b1df08" 13194139535379 true] [17592186346678 1145 "The first four terms of the series are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{3!} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{6}}{5!} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-\\frac{{x}^{8}}{7!}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can express these terms using a common format, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{(-1)^{0}{x}^{2\\cdot (0+1)}}{(2\\cdot 0+1)!} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{(-1)^{1}{x}^{2\\cdot (1+1)}}{(2\\cdot 1+1)!} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{(-1)^{2}{x}^{2\\cdot (2+1)}}{(2\\cdot 2+1)!} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{(-1)^{3}{x}^{2\\cdot (3+1)}}{(2\\cdot 3+1)!}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe deduce that the general formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2(n+1)}}{(2n+1)!}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2(n+1)}}{(2n+1)!}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535379 true] [17592186346679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346680 13194139535379 true] [17592186346679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346681 13194139535379 true] [17592186346679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346682 13194139535379 true] [17592186346679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346683 13194139535379 true] [17592186346679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346684 13194139535379 true] [17592186346679 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535379 true] [17592186346679 1041 "selection" 13194139535379 true] [17592186346679 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346681 13194139535379 true] [17592186346679 1110 #uuid "76568bd1-6b96-5818-ba26-eced006ce667" 13194139535379 true] [17592186346680 1034 "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{x}^{n+2}}{(n+1)!}" 13194139535379 true] [17592186346680 1103 #e